# Decimal addition with double operands

Adds 1.20 and 2.25 in both operand orders to verify the f64 value converts
into an exact decimal result, producing 3.45 either way. A further case
adds an f64 hundredth to 0.02 to verify the inexact binary value still
converts exactly, producing 0.03.

>>> source
decimal_left: decimal = 1.20
double_right: double = 2.25

// Verifies the Decimal/Double conversion.
decimal_plus_double: decimal = decimal_left + double_right
print(decimal_plus_double)

// Verifies the same conversion with the operand order reversed.
double_plus_decimal: decimal = double_right + decimal_left
print(double_plus_decimal)

hundredth_double: double = 0.01

// Verifies an f64 hundredth converts exactly when added to a decimal.
mixed_hundredth: decimal = hundredth_double + 0.02
print(mixed_hundredth)

<<< stdout
3.45
3.45
0.03

<<< stderr
